# Moved from bootstrap/examples/decl-ctx-cycle-functor.moss. Verdicts below credited to the
# oracle are the old Rocq oracle's (moss_m2, removed when moss-ref replaced
# it), so they are historical; the suite checks the current verdicts.
# DeclsForm (AUDIT-CHANGES #74; criteria section 7): every declared context
# forms as written, used or not. A and B nest in a cycle, and only an
# abstract functor's result, which nothing applies or binds, lists A.
# Verdicts: oracle rejects ("context `A` nests in a cycle"); native
# rejects ("context expansion is recursive or nested too deeply: `A`");
# Audit before accepts (nothing forms A); now rejects (A's items have no
# finite ItemsEntries derivation).
val x: ();
context A = x, B;
context B = A;
functor F: x -> A;
fn main() {}
